 "titulo": {
  "estudio": "Así que, por eso",
  "alumno": "So, that's why"
 },
 "intro": "Connectors to tell the result, and «tan… que» for a result that comes from intensity.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "así que",
   "significado": "so",
   "pron": "a-SI ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It joins a cause with its result in speech: «perdí el autobús, así que llegué tarde».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por lo tanto",
   "significado": "therefore",
   "pron": "por lo TAN-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is more formal than «así que». It is used in written texts and speeches.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "entonces",
   "significado": "so; then",
   "pron": "en-TON-thes",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is used to draw a conclusion: «Entonces, nos vamos». It sounds th in Spain: en-TON-thes.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "o sea que",
   "significado": "so; in other words",
   "pron": "o SE-a ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is very common in speech to draw a conclusion: «o sea que no vienes».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "total que",
   "significado": "so in the end (colloquial)",
   "pron": "to-TAL ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It sums up a story in an informal tone: «total, que llegamos tarde».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "por consiguiente",
   "significado": "consequently (formal)",
   "pron": "por kon-si-GYEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Very formal: it appears in reports and letters, almost never in speech.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tan",
   "significado": "so (with an adjective or adverb)",
   "pron": "tan",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It goes before an adjective or adverb and never changes: «tan cansado», «tan deprisa».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tanto",
   "significado": "so much; so many",
   "pron": "TAN-to",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "With a noun it agrees with it: «tanta gente», «tantos coches». After a verb it does not change.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sueño",
   "significado": "sleepiness; dream",
   "pron": "SWE-nyo",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Tener sueño» means to feel sleepy. It is also what you see while you sleep.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "despertador",
   "significado": "alarm clock",
   "pron": "des-per-ta-DOR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "noun",
   "genero": "m",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It comes from «despertar». The stress is at the end: des-per-ta-DOR.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "enfadado",
   "significado": "angry",
   "pron": "en-fa-DA-do",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adjective",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "You say «estar enfadado». In the Americas you also hear «enojado».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sonar",
   "significado": "to ring; to sound",
   "pron": "so-NAR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is irregular: «suena», but «sonó» does not change. The alarm clock «suena».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "sales",
   "significado": "you leave (salir)",
   "pron": "SA-les",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Present of «salir», for «tú». Here it means you leave work later today.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "pasará",
   "significado": "will happen (pasar)",
   "pron": "pa-sa-RA",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "verb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Future of «pasar». Here it means the same thing will happen tomorrow.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
